# Staging first

Ship every code change through `staging` before `main`. Staging is https://staging.extrablatt.app (Railway `staging` environment). Production is https://reader.extrablatt.app from `main`.

## Branch and PRs

- Branch off `origin/staging`, not `main`.
- Push the feature branch, then merge to `staging` (PR base `staging`).
- Do not merge app/docs/workflow changes straight to `main`.
- After staging looks right, promote with a PR from `staging` into `main`.

```text
# ❌ BAD — PR into production
git checkout -b cursor/fix-foo origin/main
# open PR → main

# ✅ GOOD — staging, then production
git fetch origin staging
git checkout -b cursor/fix-foo origin/staging
# open PR → staging
# later: PR staging → main
```

## Do not

- Point new PRs at `main` by default
- Push commits to `main` to “just get it live”
- Treat a green staging deploy as a production deploy
